From 121ad79356b2cf6db6991c81008b8d05a968c54b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 17:55:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] gap-closing WIP: revive the hc_combine_norm prefill
 fusion (matcher + 3-D out_xn)

Prototype for closing-the-gap item 1 (HC combine+norm).  The delivery's
hc_combine_norm graph-optimizer matcher had been dormant: it never fired on
qwen4exp.  Root-caused and fixed:

* build_hc_combine emitted the scatter-weight VIEW after the block_out REPEAT,
  so the fusion window [repeat, mul, add, rms, mul(gamma)] had a RESHAPE with an
  external view_src between the repeat and the mul; ggml_can_fuse_subgraph_ext
  rejected it.  Emit the w view before the repeat so the window is contiguous.
* the matcher's ok_f required the pre-rebase 2-D gamma-mul shape; the current
  graph's gamma-mul is 3-D [n_embd, hc, n_tok].  Accept either shape.
* ggml_cuda_op_hc_combine_norm asserted out_xn->ne[0] == n_embd*hc; relax to the
  element count (the kernel's row-major addressing is layout-identical).
* add LLAMA_FUSED_DSV4_HC_PRE/_POST env toggles + LLAMA_HC_CN_DEBUG traces so the
  matcher arm can be A/B'd against the DSV4_HC_POST op.

Measured on gfx1151, qwen4exp IQ4_NL, prefill-only, matcher arm
(LLAMA_FUSED_DSV4_HC_POST=0) vs the DSV4_HC_POST arm:
  pp2048 834.5 vs 822.1, pp8192 835.0 vs 827.7, pp32768 811.5 vs 797.1 (+1-2%).
Same-seed greedy text identical on a smoke prompt; full purity gate not yet run.
Default is unchanged (fused_dsv4_hc_post still true) - the matcher is inert
unless the env disables the op.
